# Star Castle sound board -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Cinematronics vector games carry a small audio board of their own, driven from the
# CPU board's output latch: the latch bits arrive here as ports (OUT_0 ... OUT_7, MAME's
# TTL_INPUT names), and the board's sound goes out to a final amplifier that MAME does
# not simulate and this file therefore does not contain.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/cinematronics/nl_starcas.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(starcas). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Aaron Giles (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/cinematronics/nl_starcas.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
# The sheet numbers its ICs IC1, IC2 ...; they are written U1, U2 ... here, because the
# checker files every IC under a U designator.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 34: #define HLE_BACKGROUND_VCO 1 -> 0 (high-level stand-in for a real circuit)
# line 35: #define HLE_LASER_VCO 1 -> 0 (high-level stand-in for a real circuit)
# line 36: #define ENABLE_FRONTIERS 1 -> 0 (solver partitioning only)
# line 765: NET_C(GND, IC28.8, IC28.9, IC28.10, IC28.11) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unconnected inputs" block
# line 767: NET_C(GND, IC6.3) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unconnected inputs" block
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_0), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_1), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_2), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_3), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_4), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_7)
#
# Left out by MAME (commented out at TAG, so not in this file either):
#   line 220: RES(R120, RES_K(390)) -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 221: RES(R121, RES_K(15))  -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 222: RES(R122, 150)        -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 223: RES(R123, RES_K(22))  -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 224: RES(R124, 150)        -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 231: CAP(C2, CAP_U(25))      // electrolytic
#   line 232: CAP(C4, CAP_U(25))      // electrolytic
#   line 233: CAP(C5, CAP_U(25))      // electrolytic
#   line 234: CAP(C7, CAP_U(25))      // electrolytic
#   line 235: CAP(C9, CAP_U(25))      // electrolytic
#   line 268: CAP(C43, CAP_U(0.68))   // film -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 269: CAP(C44, CAP_P(470))    // disk -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 270: CAP(C45, CAP_P(470))    // disk -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 271: CAP(C46, CAP_P(470))    // disk -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 272: CAP(C47, CAP_U(0.005))  // disk -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 275: D_1N4003(D1)            // not needed
#   line 276: D_1N4003(D2)            // not needed
#   line 277: D_1N4003(D3)            // not needed
#   line 278: D_1N4003(D4)            // not needed
#   line 306: Q_2N6107(Q17)           // PNP -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 307: Q_2N6292(Q18)           // NPN -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 321: TTL_7815_DIP(IC4)       // +15V Regulator -- not needed
#   line 322: TTL_7915_DIP(IC5)       // -15V Regulator -- not needed
#   line 392: TL081_DIP(IC25)         // Op. Amp. -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#
# MAME's file says it is derived from the schematics and parts list in the Star Castle
# manual. Compared with sheet 2 of the audio board, 72-10861-02 (doc 7f01a2f3c820 p87),
# 2026-10-19: the noise generator (IC14 S2688, IC15 follower, C16-C18, R28), the +2.2V
# reference (Q2, R29-R31, C19), the 60 Hz 555 IC16 (R32, R33, C20, C21), the laser VCO
# (IC17 566, C22-C25, R41-R43, Q5, R44-R46, D10) with the 74LS393 IC12 and its taps
# R47-R49, the CA3080 IC18's input network (R57-R62), the summing follower IC26 (R127, C48)
# and the output amplifier IC27 (R125, R126, the SJ junction, the 10K volume pot R128) all
# agree with MAME pin for pin and value for value. Sheet 1 (p86: latches, shift register,
# the background VCO) was not compared, nor the other four CA3080 channels or the star
# sound 555s beyond their values (R112-R119, which agree).

